Usage: gccli goals update <id> [flags]

Change an activity goal.

Arguments:
  <id>    Goal ID, as goals list prints it.

Flags:
  -h, --help                       Show context-sensitive help.
  -j, --json                       Output as JSON ($GCCLI_JSON).
      --plain                      Output as plain text (TSV) ($GCCLI_PLAIN).
      --header                     Print the column names as the first line of
                                   --plain output ($GCCLI_HEADER).
      --color="auto"               Color mode: auto, always, never
                                   ($GCCLI_COLOR).
      --account=STRING             Garmin account email ($GCCLI_ACCOUNT).
      --units="auto"               Unit system for distances, speeds, paces,
                                   elevations and weights in table and plain
                                   output: auto (Garmin profile), metric,
                                   statute_us, statute_uk ($GCCLI_UNITS).
      --version                    Print version information.

      --name=FREE-TEXT             New name, 1 to 49 characters.
      --period=PERIOD              New period: seven-days, thirty-days,
                                   one-month or annual.
      --activity-type=FREE-TEXT    New activity type key, as activities types
                                   prints it (e.g. running, cycling), or all.
      --start=DATE                 New first day of the goal (YYYY-MM-DD, today,
                                   yesterday, 3d, +30d).
      --distance=DISTANCE          Distance to cover (e.g. 50km, 30mi, 5000m).
      --duration=DURATION          Time to spend (e.g. 10h, 90m).
      --calories=KCAL              Kilocalories to burn.
      --activities=N               Number of activities to do.

